{"uid":"1adc4da434952349","name":"test_no_hat_may_report_superseded_through_the_contract_channel[False]","fullName":"tests.test_task_status_lifecycle#test_no_hat_may_report_superseded_through_the_contract_channel","historyId":"06290fabaa7748ad4669b5f426abc819","time":{"start":1792071993677,"stop":1792071993677,"duration":0},"description":"Declared is not claimable: `task_status_report_errors` refuses a\n    reported `superseded` even though the edge is in the table, because\n    `state.supersede_task()` (the engine, at a spent progressBudget) is its\n    one writer. Cure-01-05 (PRD requirement B.3/B.4, F05, #221) folds in\n    the SAME refusal's other source: `pending -> superseded` is now a\n    declared edge too (the un-reopen restore), and a hat reporting it\n    through this ordinary channel is refused exactly the same way --\n    `allow_un_reopen_restore` defaults to `False` for every hat-report\n    call site, and only `state.apply_task_status_change`'s own `source=\n    \"cure-reconciliation\"` branch ever passes `True`, a different code\n    path no report payload can flip on itself.\n\n    Cure-01-05-2 corrects this same node's own final assertion, which is\n    exactly the F05-shaped widening it was written to catch: it claimed a\n    hat's OWN variant's claim terminal stayed reportable out of `pending`\n    \"exactly as before\" cure-01-05 -- but a task sitting at `pending` was\n    never started at all, has no `in-progress`/`awaiting-validation` leg\n    behind it, and cure-01-05-2's own worker-reported probe\n    (`test_B_restore_edge_does_not_allow_worker_to_finish_untouched_task`,\n    all four of (vigilant, target) = (True, validated), (False,\n    completed), (True, skipped), (False, failed)) demonstrated the shipped\n    code applying exactly that \"still reportable\" claim to finish/skip/\n    fail a task nothing had reopened. The un-reopen edge is now refused\n    for ALL FIVE restore targets, unconditionally, out of `pending`,\n    regardless of variant or of which terminal a hat names -- own variant\n    or the other one, `completed`/`validated`/`failed`/`skipped`/\n    `superseded` alike -- and the restore stays reachable ONLY through\n    `allow_un_reopen_restore=True`.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Declared is not claimable: <code>task_status_report_errors</code> refuses a<br />\nreported <code>superseded</code> even though the edge is in the table, because<br />\n<code>state.supersede_task()</code> (the engine, at a spent progressBudget) is its<br />\none writer. Cure-01-05 (PRD requirement B.3/B.4, F05, #221) folds in<br />\nthe SAME refusal's other source: <code>pending -&gt; superseded</code> is now a<br />\ndeclared edge too (the un-reopen restore), and a hat reporting it<br />\nthrough this ordinary channel is refused exactly the same way --<br />\n<code>allow_un_reopen_restore</code> defaults to <code>False</code> for every hat-report<br />\ncall site, and only <code>state.apply_task_status_change</code>'s own <code>source= &quot;cure-reconciliation&quot;</code> branch ever passes <code>True</code>, a different code<br />\npath no report payload can flip on itself.</p>\n<pre><code>Cure-01-05-2 corrects this same node's own final assertion, which is\nexactly the F05-shaped widening it was written to catch: it claimed a\nhat's OWN variant's claim terminal stayed reportable out of `pending`\n&quot;exactly as before&quot; cure-01-05 -- but a task sitting at `pending` was\nnever started at all, has no `in-progress`/`awaiting-validation` leg\nbehind it, and cure-01-05-2's own worker-reported probe\n(`test_B_restore_edge_does_not_allow_worker_to_finish_untouched_task`,\nall four of (vigilant, target) = (True, validated), (False,\ncompleted), (True, skipped), (False, failed)) demonstrated the shipped\ncode applying exactly that &quot;still reportable&quot; claim to finish/skip/\nfail a task nothing had reopened. The un-reopen edge is now refused\nfor ALL FIVE restore targets, unconditionally, out of `pending`,\nregardless of variant or of which terminal a hat names -- own variant\nor the other one, `completed`/`validated`/`failed`/`skipped`/\n`superseded` alike -- and the restore stays reachable ONLY through\n`allow_un_reopen_restore=True`.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792071797328,"stop":1792071797328,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1792071797329,"stop":1792071797329,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1792071993658,"stop":1792071993659,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1792071993659,"stop":1792071993666,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1792071993666,"stop":1792071993666,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1792071993667,"stop":1792071993674,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachme